<% content_for :title, "submission requirements" %>
<p class="dashboard-link"><%= link_to "← desktop", root_path %></p>
<article class="guide requirements panel">
  <header>
    <%# Shown only inside requirements.txt's window, for reading it full size. %>
    <p class="guide-new-tab"><%= link_to "open the requirements in a new tab ↗", requirements_path, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %></p>
    <h1>submission requirements</h1>
  </header>

  <ul class="requirements-list">
    <li>your code is in a GitHub repository, with semi frequent commits.</li>
    <li>time is tracked using Hackatime.</li>
    <li>it must work on desktop! Windows, Mac, or Linux.</li>
    <li>it's uploaded to itch.io!</li>
    <li>a README detailing what your pet does, and how to install and run it.</li>
    <li>no AI art please, implement your own assets!</li>
    <li>personalize it! or add something unique!</li>
    <li>link to your ship message in <a href="https://hackclub.slack.com/archives/C0C51NCK1DG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">#playground-ships</a>. every ship needs its own.</li>
    <li>time spent on art can count for up to <%= Ship::ART_CAP_PERCENT %>% of your approved time.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>questions? ask in <a href="https://hackclub.slack.com/archives/C0ASBTMS82H" target="_blank" rel="noopener">#playground</a>.</p>
</article>
